      "safetyNotes": "RAZOR BLADE/SCALPEL PROTOCOL (explicit for Lessons 2 and 5): 1) Only one designated Cutter per group of 4-5 handles the blade, and the role rotates only when the blade is placed down in the tray. 2) Blades are kept in a labelled tray or blade-holder or mounted in a handle, never passed hand to hand; place the blade on the tray and let the next person pick it up. 3) Always cut away from the body and fingers, on a tile or cardboard board, with the flower held by forceps or a pencil and not in the palm. 4) Learners stand or sit upright and keep the bench clear of bags and food. 5) Teacher counts blades out and in at the start and end (record the number on the board). 6) Any cut: stop, raise hand, teacher applies first aid from the kit. 7) Dispose of used blades in a closed container (an old tin or bottle with a slit) and never in open bins. 8) Wash hands after handling plants, since Bougainvillea bracts and some plant saps can irritate skin. Do not taste any specimen. Wear a lab coat or apron if available. Digital files are pre-downloaded; no live internet use."
